> laplace t^2 e^-t
L{t^2*e^(-t)}(s) = 2/(s + 1)^3
  region of convergence: Re(s) > -1
  one-sided: f(t) for t >= 0 (0 before)
  rules: e^(at) f(t) -> F(s - a), t^n f(t) -> (-1)^n F^(n)(s)
  check: matches int_0^inf f(t) e^(-st) dt (Gauss-Kronrod) at s = -1/2, 1/2, 3: max relative difference 4.4e-16
> laplace e^(-2t) cos(3t)
L{e^(-2t)*cos(3t)}(s) = (s + 2)/(s^2 + 4s + 13)
  region of convergence: Re(s) > -2
  one-sided: f(t) for t >= 0 (0 before)
  rules: e^(at) f(t) -> F(s - a), sin/cos table
  check: matches int_0^inf f(t) e^(-st) dt (Gauss-Kronrod) at s = -3/2, -1/2, 2: max relative difference 2.6e-13
> laplace t sin(t)
L{t*sin(t)}(s) = 2s/(s^2 + 1)^2
  region of convergence: Re(s) > 0
  one-sided: f(t) for t >= 0 (0 before)
  rules: t^n f(t) -> (-1)^n F^(n)(s), sin/cos table
  check: matches int_0^inf f(t) e^(-st) dt (Gauss-Kronrod) at s = 1/2, 3/2, 4: max relative difference 2.5e-16
> laplace sin(t)^2
L{sin(t)^2}(s) = 2/(s*(s^2 + 4))
  region of convergence: Re(s) > 0
  one-sided: f(t) for t >= 0 (0 before)
  rules: sin/cos table, power reduction
  check: matches int_0^inf f(t) e^(-st) dt (Gauss-Kronrod) at s = 1/2, 3/2, 4: max relative difference 1.2e-16
> laplace sinh(2t)
L{sinh(2t)}(s) = 2/((s + 2)*(s - 2))
  region of convergence: Re(s) > 2
  one-sided: f(t) for t >= 0 (0 before)
  rules: sinh/cosh table
  check: matches int_0^inf f(t) e^(-st) dt (Gauss-Kronrod) at s = 5/2, 7/2, 6: max relative difference 0
> laplace cosh(3t)
L{cosh(3t)}(s) = s/((s + 3)*(s - 3))
  region of convergence: Re(s) > 3
  one-sided: f(t) for t >= 0 (0 before)
  rules: sinh/cosh table
  check: matches int_0^inf f(t) e^(-st) dt (Gauss-Kronrod) at s = 7/2, 9/2, 7: max relative difference 2.1e-16
> laplace sqrt(t)
L{sqrt(t)}(s) = sqrt(pi)/(2s^(3/2))
  region of convergence: Re(s) > 0
  one-sided: f(t) for t >= 0 (0 before)
  rules: t^p -> Gamma(p + 1)/s^(p + 1)
  check: matches int_0^inf f(t) e^(-st) dt (Gauss-Kronrod) at s = 1/2, 3/2, 4: max relative difference 1.1e-13
> laplace (t - 1) u(t - 1)
L{(t - 1)*u(t - 1)}(s) = e^(-s)/s^2
  region of convergence: Re(s) > 0
  one-sided: f(t) for t >= 0 (0 before)
  rules: linearity, t^n f(t) -> (-1)^n F^(n)(s), u(t - a) f(t - a) -> e^(-as) F(s)
  check: matches int_0^inf f(t) e^(-st) dt (Gauss-Kronrod) at s = 1/2, 3/2, 4: max relative difference 2.8e-16
> laplace delta(t - 3)
L{delta(t - 3)}(s) = e^(-3s)
  region of convergence: every s (f is zero after a finite time)
  one-sided: f(t) for t >= 0 (0 before)
  rules: delta(t - a) -> e^(-as)
  check: matches int_0^inf f(t) e^(-st) dt (Gauss-Kronrod) at s = 1/2, 3/2, 4 (delta terms left out): max relative difference 0
> laplace e^(a t)
L{e^(a*t)}(s) = 1/(s - a)
  region of convergence: Re(s) > a
  one-sided: f(t) for t >= 0 (0 before)
  rules: e^(at) f(t) -> F(s - a)
  check: matches int_0^inf f(t) e^(-st) dt (Gauss-Kronrod) at s = 6/5, 11/5, 47/10 with a = 7/10: max relative difference 2.2e-16
> laplace sin(w t)
L{sin(w*t)}(s) = w/(s^2 + w^2)
  region of convergence: Re(s) > 0
  one-sided: f(t) for t >= 0 (0 before)
  rules: sin/cos table
  check: matches int_0^inf f(t) e^(-st) dt (Gauss-Kronrod) at s = 1/2, 3/2, 4 with w = 7/10: max relative difference 2.2e-16
> laplace e^(-t) sin(t) t s
  note: the last word t is read as the variable (write *t to multiply by it)
L{e^(-t)*sin(t)}(s) = 1/(s^2 + 2s + 2)
  region of convergence: Re(s) > -1
  one-sided: f(t) for t >= 0 (0 before)
  rules: e^(at) f(t) -> F(s - a), sin/cos table
  check: matches int_0^inf f(t) e^(-st) dt (Gauss-Kronrod) at s = -1/2, 1/2, 3: max relative difference 1.8e-16
> laplace {1 if t < 1, -1 otherwise} period 2
L{t < 1 ? 1 : -1}(s) = (1/s - 2*e^(-s)/s + e^(-2s)/s)/(1 - e^(-2s))
  f is the periodic extension of its values on [0, 2)
  region of convergence: Re(s) > 0
  one-sided: f(t) for t >= 0 (0 before)
  rules: linearity, u(t - a) f(t - a) -> e^(-as) F(s), piecewise as steps, periodic: F(s) = F_T(s)/(1 - e^(-Ts))
  check: matches int_0^inf f(t) e^(-st) dt (Gauss-Kronrod) at s = 1/2, 3/2, 4: max relative difference 2.6e-16
> ilaplace 1/(s^2 + 1)
L^-1{1/(s^2 + 1)}(t) = sin(t)
  poles: s = +-i
  for t >= 0 (0 before): the right-sided inverse, region of convergence Re(s) > 0 (right of every pole)
  check: transformed back (Gauss-Kronrod), it matches F at s = 1, 2, 7/2: max relative difference 1.4e-16
> ilaplace (s + 3)/((s + 1)*(s + 2))
L^-1{(s + 3)/((s + 1)*(s + 2))}(t) = 2*e^(-t) - e^(-2t)
  poles: s = -1, -2
  for t >= 0 (0 before): the right-sided inverse, region of convergence Re(s) > -1 (right of every pole)
  check: transformed back (Gauss-Kronrod), it matches F at s = 1, 2, 7/2: max relative difference 1.3e-16
> ilaplace 1/(s^2 + 2s + 5)
L^-1{1/(s^2 + 2s + 5)}(t) = e^(-t)*sin(2t)/2
  poles: s = -1 +- 2i
  for t >= 0 (0 before): the right-sided inverse, region of convergence Re(s) > -1 (right of every pole)
  check: transformed back (Gauss-Kronrod), it matches F at s = 1, 2, 7/2: max relative difference 2.2e-16
> ilaplace 1/(s + 1)^3
L^-1{1/(s + 1)^3}(t) = t^2*e^(-t)/2
  poles: s = -1 (triple)
  for t >= 0 (0 before): the right-sided inverse, region of convergence Re(s) > -1 (right of every pole)
  check: transformed back (Gauss-Kronrod), it matches F at s = 1, 2, 7/2: max relative difference 1.6e-16
> ilaplace 1/(s^2 - 4)
L^-1{1/(s^2 - 4)}(t) = sinh(2t)/2
  poles: s = -2, 2
  for t >= 0 (0 before): the right-sided inverse, region of convergence Re(s) > 2 (right of every pole)
  check: transformed back (Gauss-Kronrod), it matches F at s = 3, 4, 11/2: max relative difference 1.7e-16
> ilaplace e^(-2s)/s^2
L^-1{e^(-2s)/s^2}(t) = (t - 2)*u(t - 2)
  poles: s = 0 (double)
  for t >= 0 (0 before): the right-sided inverse, region of convergence Re(s) > 0 (right of every pole)
  check: transformed back (Gauss-Kronrod), it matches F at s = 1, 2, 7/2: max relative difference 7.3e-16
> ilaplace 1/sqrt(s)
L^-1{1/sqrt(s)}(t) = 1/(sqrt(pi)*sqrt(t))
  for t >= 0 (0 before): the right-sided inverse, region of convergence Re(s) > 0 (right of every pole)
  check: transformed back (Gauss-Kronrod), it matches F at s = 1, 2, 7/2: max relative difference 4.7e-14
> ilaplace s/(s^2 + w^2)
L^-1{s/(s^2 + w^2)}(t) = cos(w*t)
  for t >= 0 (0 before): the right-sided inverse, region of convergence Re(s) > 0 (right of every pole)
  assuming w > 0
  check: transformed back (Gauss-Kronrod), it matches F at s = 1, 2, 7/2 with w = 7/10: max relative difference 4e-16
> ilaplace (s^2 + 1)/(s^2 + 3)
L^-1{(s^2 + 1)/(s^2 + 3)}(t) = delta(t) - 2sqrt(3)*sin(sqrt(3)*t)/3
  poles: s = +-sqrt(3)*i
  for t >= 0 (0 before): the right-sided inverse, region of convergence Re(s) > 0 (right of every pole)
  the constant part of F gives delta(t)
  check: transformed back (Gauss-Kronrod), it matches F at s = 1, 2, 7/2: max relative difference 2.2e-16
> laplace solve y'' + y = sin(t), y(0) = 0, y'(0) = 1
y'' + y = sin(t), y(0) = 0, y'(0) = 1
  transformed: (s^2 + 1)Y(s) - 1 = 1/(s^2 + 1)
  Y(s) = (s^2 + 2)/(s^2 + 1)^2
  y(t) = -t*cos(t)/2 + 3sin(t)/2    for t >= 0
  poles of Y: +-i (double)
  check: residual of the equation at 201 points of [0, 10]: max 8.3e-16; initial values hold (max difference 0)
  check: a numeric solution (RK4, h = 1/1000) agrees at 20 points of [0, 10]: max difference 1.4e-13
> y'' = -y + sin(t)
> y(0) = 0
> y'(0) = 1
> dsolve y from 0 to 3
y'' = -y + sin(t), y(0) = 0, y'(0) = 1
  linear with constant coefficients (eigenvalues 0 ± 1i), but no closed form was found for the forcing: numeric only
  numeric (Dormand-Prince 5(4), adaptive, 88 steps, tolerance 1e-10); a 1000x looser solve differs by 4.2e-08
