> laplace solve y'' + 3y' + 2y = u(t - 1)
y'' + 3y' + 2y = u(t - 1), y(0) = 0, y'(0) = 0
  note: y(0), y'(0) not given: taken as 0
  transformed: (s^2 + 3s + 2)Y(s) = e^(-s)/s
  Y(s) = e^(-s)/(s*(s + 1)*(s + 2))
  y(t) = (1/2 - e^(1 - t) + e^(-2(t - 1))/2)*u(t - 1)    for t >= 0
  poles of Y: 0, -1, -2
  check: residual of the equation at 201 points of [0, 10]: max 2.2e-16; initial values hold (max difference 0)
  check: a numeric solution (RK4, h = 1/1000) agrees at 20 points of [0, 10]: max difference 2.2e-14
> laplace solve y' + 2y = e^(-t), y(0) = 1
y' + 2y = e^(-t), y(0) = 1
  transformed: (s + 2)Y(s) - 1 = 1/(s + 1)
  Y(s) = 1/(s + 1)
  y(t) = e^(-t)    for t >= 0
  poles of Y: -1
  check: residual of the equation at 201 points of [0, 10]: max 1.1e-16; initial values hold (max difference 0)
  check: a numeric solution (RK4, h = 1/1000) agrees at 20 points of [0, 10]: max difference 1.7e-14
> ztrans 0.5^n
Z{(1/2)^n}(z) = 2z/(2z - 1)
  in powers of z^-1: 1/(1 - (1/2)z^-1)
  region of convergence: |z| > 1/2
  one-sided: x[n] for n >= 0
  rules: a^n x[n] -> X(z/a)
  check: matches sum_n x[n] z^-n (79 terms) at z = 3/2, 3, 13/2: max relative difference 3.7e-16
> ztrans a^n u[n]
Z{a^n*u[n]}(z) = z/(z - a)
  region of convergence: |z| > abs(a)
  one-sided: x[n] for n >= 0
  rules: a^n x[n] -> X(z/a)
  check: matches sum_n x[n] z^-n (88 terms) at z = 17/10, 17/5, 71/10 with a = 7/10: max relative difference 2e-16
> ztrans n^2
Z{n^2}(z) = (z^2 + z)/(z - 1)^3
  in powers of z^-1: (z^-1 + z^-2)/(1 - 3z^-1 + 3z^-2 - z^-3)
  region of convergence: |z| > 1
  one-sided: x[n] for n >= 0
  rules: n x[n] -> -z X'(z)
  check: matches sum_n x[n] z^-n (111 terms) at z = 2, 4, 8: max relative difference 1.5e-16
> ztrans n 0.5^n
Z{n*(1/2)^n}(z) = 2z/(2z - 1)^2
  in powers of z^-1: (1/2)z^-1/(1 - z^-1 + (1/4)z^-2)
  region of convergence: |z| > 1/2
  one-sided: x[n] for n >= 0
  rules: a^n x[n] -> X(z/a), n x[n] -> -z X'(z)
  check: matches sum_n x[n] z^-n (83 terms) at z = 3/2, 3, 13/2: max relative difference 1.5e-16
> ztrans cos(pi n/3)
Z{cos(pi*n/3)}(z) = (2z^2 - z)/(2(z^2 - z + 1))
  in powers of z^-1: (1 - (1/2)z^-1)/(1 - z^-1 + z^-2)
  region of convergence: |z| > 1
  one-sided: x[n] for n >= 0
  rules: cos/sin table
  check: matches sum_n x[n] z^-n (100 terms) at z = 2, 4, 8: max relative difference 0
> ztrans u[n - 3]
Z{u[n - 3]}(z) = 1/(z^2*(z - 1))
  in powers of z^-1: z^-3/(1 - z^-1)
  region of convergence: |z| > 1
  one-sided: x[n] for n >= 0
  rules: x[n - k] u[n - k] -> z^-k X(z)
  check: matches sum_n x[n] z^-n (103 terms) at z = 2, 4, 8: max relative difference 0
> ztrans 1/n!
Z{1/n!}(z) = e^(1/z)
  region of convergence: |z| > 0
  one-sided: x[n] for n >= 0
  rules: a^n/n! -> e^(a/z)
  check: matches sum_n x[n] z^-n (61 terms) at z = 1, 2, 5: max relative difference 2.7e-16
> iztrans z/(z - 0.5)
Z^-1{z/(z - 1/2)}[n] = (1/2)^n    for n >= 0
  poles: z = 1/2
  taken as causal (right-sided): region of convergence |z| > 1/2
  long division in z^-1: 1, 1/2, 1/4, 1/8, 1/16, 1/32, 1/64, 1/128, ...
  check: the closed form equals the long division for n = 0..31 (max difference 0)
> iztrans z/((z - 1)*(z - 0.5))
Z^-1{z/((z - 1)*(z - 1/2))}[n] = -2(1/2)^n + 2    for n >= 0
  poles: z = 1, 1/2
  taken as causal (right-sided): region of convergence |z| > 1
  long division in z^-1: 0, 1, 3/2, 7/4, 15/8, 31/16, 63/32, 127/64, ...
  check: the closed form equals the long division for n = 0..31 (max difference 0)
> iztrans z^2/(z^2 - z + 0.5)
Z^-1{z^2/(z^2 - z + 1/2)}[n] = (sqrt(2)/2)^n*(cos(pi*n/4) + sin(pi*n/4))    for n >= 0
  poles: z = 1/2 +- i/2
  taken as causal (right-sided): region of convergence |z| > sqrt(2)/2
  long division in z^-1: 1, 1, 1/2, 0, -1/4, -1/4, -1/8, 0, ...
  check: the closed form equals the long division for n = 0..31 (max difference 1.1e-16)
> iztrans z/(z - 1)^2
Z^-1{z/(z - 1)^2}[n] = n    for n >= 0
  poles: z = 1 (double)
  taken as causal (right-sided): region of convergence |z| > 1
  long division in z^-1: 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, ...
  check: the closed form equals the long division for n = 0..31 (max difference 0)
> iztrans (z + 1)/z^2
Z^-1{(z + 1)/z^2}[n] = delta[n - 1] + delta[n - 2]    for n >= 0
  poles: z = 0 (double)
  taken as causal (right-sided): region of convergence |z| > 0
  long division in z^-1: 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, ...
  check: the closed form equals the long division for n = 0..31 (max difference 0)
> iztrans e^(2/z)
Z^-1{e^(2/z)}[n] = 2^n/n!    for n >= 0
  taken as causal (right-sided): region of convergence outside every pole
> zsolve y[n+2] = y[n+1] + y[n], y[0] = 0, y[1] = 1
y[n+2] = y[n+1] + y[n], y[0] = 0, y[1] = 1
  transformed: (z^2 - z - 1)Y(z) - (z) = 0
  Y(z) = z/(z^2 - z - 1)
  y[n] = sqrt(5)*((1 + sqrt(5))/2)^n/5 - sqrt(5)*((1 - sqrt(5))/2)^n/5    for n >= 0
  poles of Y: (1 + sqrt(5))/2, (1 - sqrt(5))/2
  check: iterating the recurrence gives the same y[0..39] (max relative difference 1.2e-15)
> zsolve x[n+1] = 2x[n] + n, x[0] = 1
x[n+1] = 2x[n] + n, x[0] = 1
  transformed: (z - 2)Y(z) - (z) = z/(z - 1)^2
  Y(z) = (z^3 - 2z^2 + 2z)/((z - 1)^2*(z - 2))
  x[n] = -n - 1 + 2*2^n    for n >= 0
  poles of Y: 1 (double), 2
  check: iterating the recurrence gives the same x[0..39] (max relative difference 0)
> zsolve y[n] = 0.5 y[n-1] + 1, y[0] = 2
y[n] = 0.5 y[n-1] + 1, y[0] = 2
  the recurrence holds for n >= 1
  transformed: (z - 1/2)Y(z) - (2z) = z/(z - 1)
  Y(z) = 2z/(z - 1)
  y[n] = 2    for n >= 0
  poles of Y: 1
  check: iterating the recurrence gives the same y[0..39] (max relative difference 0)
> f[0] = 1
> f[k+1] = 2f[k] + k
> closed f
f[n]
  = 2*2^n - n - 1
  method: affine recurrence (particular solution)
  check: equals direct iteration at all 61 points of the domain
> tf y[n] = 0.9 y[n-1] + x[n]
transfer function of y[n] = 0.9 y[n-1] + x[n] (zero initial state)
  input x, output y: H(z) = Y(z)/X(z)
  H(z) = 10z/(10z - 9)
       = 1/(1 - (9/10)z^-1)
  poles: 9/10
  zeros: 0
  stable (BIBO): every pole inside the unit circle (max |p| = 9/10)
  causal: yes (deg numerator <= deg denominator)
  impulse response h[n] = (9/10)^n    for n >= 0
  DC gain H(1) = 10
  frequency response H(e^(iw)), w in radians per sample:
    w          |H|          dB         phase (deg)
    0          10           20         0
    pi/8       2.60805      8.326      -63.93
    pi/4       1.36436      2.699      -60.26
    pi/2       0.743294     -2.577     -41.99
    3pi/4      0.569545     -4.889     -21.25
    pi         0.526316     -5.575     0
  -3 dB (gain 10/sqrt(2)) at w = 0.105458 rad/sample
    = 0.0167842 of the sample rate
  as C (direct form I; x1 = x[n-1], y1 = y[n-1], ...):
    float y = x + 0.9f*y1;
    y1 = y;
> tf y[n] = (x[n] + x[n-1] + x[n-2])/3
transfer function of y[n] = (x[n] + x[n-1] + x[n-2])/3 (zero initial state)
  input x, output y: H(z) = Y(z)/X(z)
  H(z) = (z^2 + z + 1)/(3z^2)
       = 1/3 + (1/3)z^-1 + (1/3)z^-2
  poles: 0 (double)
  zeros: -1/2 +- sqrt(3)i/2
  stable (BIBO): every pole inside the unit circle (max |p| = 0)
  causal: yes (deg numerator <= deg denominator)
  impulse response h[n] = delta[n]/3 + delta[n - 1]/3 + delta[n - 2]/3    for n >= 0
  DC gain H(1) = 1
  frequency response H(e^(iw)), w in radians per sample:
    w          |H|          dB         phase (deg)
    0          1            0          0
    pi/8       0.949253     -0.4524    -22.5
    pi/4       0.804738     -1.887     -45
    pi/2       0.333333     -9.542     -90
    3pi/4      0.138071     -17.2      45
    pi         0.333333     -9.542     0
  -3 dB (gain 1/sqrt(2)) at w = 0.975613 rad/sample
    = 0.155274 of the sample rate
  as C (direct form I; x1 = x[n-1], y1 = y[n-1], ...):
    float y = 0.333333333f*x + 0.333333333f*x1 + 0.333333333f*x2;
    x2 = x1; x1 = x;
> tf y[n] - 1.5y[n-1] + 0.5y[n-2] = x[n]
transfer function of y[n] - 1.5y[n-1] + 0.5y[n-2] = x[n] (zero initial state)
  input x, output y: H(z) = Y(z)/X(z)
  H(z) = 2z^2/((z - 1)*(2z - 1))
       = 1/(1 - (3/2)z^-1 + (1/2)z^-2)
  poles: 1, 1/2
  zeros: 0 (x2)
  marginally stable at best: a pole on the unit circle (|p| = 1): bounded input can give unbounded output
  causal: yes (deg numerator <= deg denominator)
  impulse response h[n] = 2 - (1/2)^n    for n >= 0
  frequency response H(e^(iw)), w in radians per sample:
    w          |H|          dB         phase (deg)
    0          inf          inf        (a pole)
    pi/8       4.48792      13.04      -98.33
    pi/4       1.77326      4.975      -96.18
    pi/2       0.632456     -3.979     -71.57
    3pi/4      0.386854     -8.249     -37.14
    pi         0.333333     -9.542     0
  (not BIBO stable, so no steady state: this is H on the unit circle, not what the system settles to)
  as C (direct form I; x1 = x[n-1], y1 = y[n-1], ...):
    float y = x + 1.5f*y1 - 0.5f*y2;
    y2 = y1; y1 = y;
