> radius x^n/n!
power series sum(n, 0, inf, x^n/n!) in x
  center x = 0; coefficients a_n = 1/n! of x^(n)
  radius of convergence R = inf (ratio test: |a_(n+1)/a_n| -> 0)
  interval of convergence: every x (absolutely)
  sum = e^x    for |x| < inf (e^u)
> radius x^n/n
power series sum(n, 1, inf, x^n/n) in x
  center x = 0; coefficients a_n = 1/n of x^(n)
  radius of convergence R = 1 (ratio test: |a_(n+1)/a_n| -> 1)
  at x = -1: converges conditionally (alternating series test (|a_n| decreases to 0); not absolutely: |a_n| ~ C/n (p <= 1))
  at x = 1: diverges (limit comparison with the harmonic series sum 1/n (p = 1): a_n n -> 1)
  interval of convergence: [-1, 1)
  sum = -log(1 - x)    for |x| < 1 (-log(1 - u))
